%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:update@

%9Parameters:%9

    CHECK:       Asks now whether a newer signed release is there, and
                 shows the answer (also when nothing is newer, and why a
                 check failed).

    Without an argument: whether update_check is on, when the last check
    was made and what it found.

%9Description:%9

    Tells you about new releases of erssi Shellter Edition. It never
    installs anything: an update is made from a shell with erssi --update,
    then /UPGRADE loads the new release and keeps your windows and
    channels.

    The check runs the installer that was installed with this erssi
    (shellter-install.sh --update --check --porcelain, the same check as
    erssi --check-update) in the background, so erssi goes on while it
    runs. The installer asks the repository it installed from (GitHub by
    default) for the release tags and takes the newest one with a valid
    signature by the release key it carries; a tag signed by anyone else
    is not counted. It downloads the tag list and one tag with its commit
    (about 6 KB; one more such tag for each newer one it skips, five at
    most), never the files of a release. One check runs at a time,
    and one that takes longer than two minutes is stopped.

    erssi checks by itself only with update_check on (/HELP update_check).
    An erssi that the installer did not install (a distribution package,
    a build of your own) has nothing to run: the check says so, and you
    update it the way it was installed. In Capsicum capability mode no
    program can be started, so there is no check either; erssi
    --check-update from a shell still works.

%9Examples:%9

    /UPDATE
    /UPDATE CHECK
    /SET update_check ON

%9See also:%9 UPGRADE, UPDATE_CHECK, STATUSBAR

